# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b3), edited. solomon_roderick's first conversation.

~ start
set solomon_roderick_met
Narrator: Stone dust hangs thick in the yard, sharp as powdered chalk on your tongue. Solomon sets down a heavy iron mallet and steps between you and a small girl sorting chisels.
solomon_roderick [neutral]: Keep your boots off the dressed slate. If you want a headstone or a lintel, speak plain.
-> menu

~ menu
solomon_roderick [neutral]: State your business. Daylight never comes, and the stone doesn't cut itself.
* Ask about gravestones and stonework -> shop_open
* Ask about his masonry and the quarries -> work
* Ask about Wickermoor Village -> village
* Ask why he gives so much to the Brightsingers -> rumour
* [Insight DC 14] Note the way he watches the dark corners -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ shop_open
solomon_roderick [neutral]: Good granite and sound tools. Touch only what you can pay for.
-> menu

~ work
solomon_roderick [neutral]: My crews cut the ridge quarry, and I carve what lasts. Sofia tallies the chalk marks for me, better head for numbers than half my men.
solomon_roderick [smile]: Keep at the ledger, little bird, I'll be right here.
-> menu

~ village
solomon_roderick [weary]: Most folk here kneel to the old tree and the Mayor's Green Queen. Stone outlasts bark, if you ask me, though nobody does.
-> menu

~ rumour
solomon_roderick [neutral]: Young Weston's choir sings of morning and clean hands. When you've got a child to raise under that grinning moon, a song about dawn is worth good coin.
-> menu

~ secret_ok
Narrator: His scarred thumb rubs an old chisel mark on his forearm, and his cold brown eyes track a bent shadow by the lane.
solomon_roderick [afraid]: Every town has rot under the floorboards. Watch the folk who walk with their necks tilted and smile at the hill, I've seen their master in my sleep since I was Sofia's age.
-> menu

~ secret_fail
solomon_roderick [angry]: Staring won't lower my prices. Buy what you need or clear the yard.
-> menu
